WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.874
Lose the service mid-race, and Telo Ride rides on. The bike, the plan and the clock

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:08.876
never stop.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.653
The board keeps its last standings, and a quiet notice says they will catch up.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.120
A group class does the same: the video rolls on, the board holds, and the notice

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.215
explains why.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.413
When the service is back, the ride reconnects, takes its seat again, and the notice

00:00:40.413 --> 00:00:40.971
goes.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.607
On rejoining, the service sends the standings to that rider at once, so the board

00:00:53.607 --> 00:00:55.430
catches up within a second.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:04.983
The notice on the race, from a phone to the full screen.

00:01:14.847 --> 00:01:19.772
What the tests prove: the ride carries on, the notice shows and goes, and the board

00:01:19.772 --> 00:01:21.318
updates on rejoining.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.774
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.631
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:34.631 --> 00:01:36.302
every hill and interval.

00:01:36.647 --> 00:01:41.825
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:41.825 --> 00:01:47.273
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:50.263
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:53.101
A custom workout lives under Profile.
